1
00:05:46,666 --> 00:05:52,666
A city divided. Their love will challenge everything.

2
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:39,333
West Side Story is a drama, romance, crime film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Two youngsters from rival New York City gangs fall in love, but tensions
between their respective friends build toward tragedy.

4
00:23:06,666 --> 00:23:12,666
Tony, played by Ansel Elgort.

5
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:59,333
María, played by Rachel Zegler.

6
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Anita, played by Ariana DeBose.

7
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
Bernardo, played by David Alvarez.

8
00:46:13,333 --> 00:46:19,333
Riff, played by Mike Faist.

9
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Officer Krupke, played by Brian d'Arcy James.

10
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
West Side Story is a 2021 American musical romantic drama film produced and
directed by Steven Spielberg from a screenplay by Tony Kushner.

11
01:03:33,333 --> 01:03:39,333
The second feature-length adaptation of the 1957 stage musical, which was itself inspired by William Shakespeare's play Romeo and Juliet, it stars Ansel
Elgort and Rachel Zegler, the latter making her film debut, with Ariana DeBose, David Alvarez, Mike Faist, and Rita Moreno in supporting roles.

12
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
Moreno, who starred in the 1961 film adaptation, also served
as an executive producer alongside Kushner.

13
01:15:06,666 --> 01:15:12,666
The film features music composed by Leonard
Bernstein with lyrics by Stephen Sondheim.

14
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
The film entered development in 2014 at 20th Century Studios (then-named 20th
Century Fox); Kushner began writing the screenplay in 2017.

15
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
In January 2018, Spielberg was hired and casting began that September.

16
01:32:26,666 --> 01:32:32,666
Justin Peck choreographed the dance sequences.

17
01:38:13,333 --> 01:38:19,333
Principal photography occurred in New York and New Jersey;
filming began in July 2019 and ran for two months.

18
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
West Side Story had its world premiere at Jazz at Lincoln Center's Rose Theater in
New York City on November 29, 2021, three days after Sondheim's death.

19
01:49:46,666 --> 01:49:52,666
The film was later theatrically distributed by 20th Century Studios in the United States
on December 10, after being delayed a year due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

20
01:55:33,333 --> 01:55:39,333
The film received critical acclaim with praise for the performances of the cast, Spielberg's direction, the musical
numbers, the visual style and the cinematography, with some critics deeming it superior to the 1961 film.

21
02:01:20,000 --> 02:01:26,000
It was named one of the top ten films of 2021 by the National
Board of Review and the American Film Institute.

22
02:07:06,666 --> 02:07:12,666
Among its multiple awards and nominations, it received seven nominations at the 94th Academy
Awards, including Best Picture, with DeBose winning Best Supporting Actress.

23
02:12:53,333 --> 02:12:59,333
However, the film was a box office bomb, grossing only $76 million against a $100
million production budget, and an estimated $300 million break even target.

24
02:18:40,000 --> 02:18:46,000
Since its release, it has been cited as one of the best musical films of all time
as well as one of the best films of the 2020s and the 21st century.

25
02:24:26,666 --> 02:24:32,666
The film explores themes of new york city, dancing,
dance, street gang, love at first sight.

26
02:30:13,333 --> 02:30:19,333
The tone is emotional.
